{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "ScmDynamicsColumn",
  "description": "The non-physics half of EqWeather-SCM (PLAN.md 3.1): the five WRF-ARW column-dynamics components mounted by reference on ONE shared column state of the em_scm_xy reference run and coupled as WRF couples them, at derivative level. WRFColumnGeometry turns the dynamical state (geopotential, moist theta, moisture, the hydrostatic base state) into heights, the eta interpolation weights and the perturbation pressure; those feed WRFRayleighDamping (z_w -> ze_in), WRFPerturbationCoriolis (z_w, w_above, w_below), WRFCurvature (w_above, w_below) and WRFVerticalMomentum (p_p -> p_p_in) through variable_map param_to_var edges into the components' additive <x>_in coupling-target parameters, which the mount-edge libraries couplings/tests/scmdyn_couple_*_inputs.esm lower the input_<x> rewrite targets to. The shared state enters every mount through the dump library couplings/tests/scmdyn_step900_state_inputs.esm; column-constant scalars (mu', mu_b, p_top, f, e, sina, cosa, dampcoef, zdamp) are prescribed in this model and coupled in, because a parent test cannot set a mounted component's parameter. This model exposes the total non-physics tendency of each prognostic variable -- u, v: Coriolis + curvature + sponge; w: vertical pressure gradient and buoyancy + Coriolis + curvature + sponge; theta_m: sponge; phi: g w -- i.e. exactly what rk_tendency adds to the physics tendencies of the column (horizontal advection and diffusion, the TKE closure and the coordinate vertical advection are identically zero here; see PLAN.md 3.1). Regime: step 900 (t = 15 h, pre-dawn deep stable night), the regime of couplings/scm_physics_column_night.esm. KNOWN LIMITS: (1) the physics suite is NOT mounted here: a top-level {ref} to couplings/scm_physics_column.esm must select one of its 10 models ([toplevel_model_ref_unresolved]), so an assembly cannot be re-used as a unit and a full EqWeather-SCM document must re-mount the nine physics components; (2) the coupled w tendency cannot be asserted tightly against WRF, because WRF's own perturbation pressure carries O(1e-2) Pa single-precision rounding that the 1/deta difference amplifies into a w tendency of the same size as the signal (see the test description); the non-pressure part of dw/dt is asserted separately and tightly.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": ["assembly", "wrf", "dynamics", "column", "eqweather-scm"]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {"type": "integer", "default": 59, "description": "Number of model layers, bound into every mount edge; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column."}
 },
 "models": {
  "Geo": {"ref": "../components/atmospheric_dynamics/wrf_arw/column_geometry.esm", "bindings": {"NLEV": "NLEV"},
   "expression_template_imports": [{"ref": "./tests/scmdyn_step900_state_inputs.esm"}]},
  "Vm": {"ref": "../components/atmospheric_dynamics/wrf_arw/vertical_momentum.esm", "bindings": {"NLEV": "NLEV"},
   "expression_template_imports": [{"ref": "./tests/scmdyn_step900_state_inputs.esm"}, {"ref": "./tests/scmdyn_couple_vm_inputs.esm"}]},
  "Cor": {"ref": "../components/atmospheric_dynamics/wrf_arw/perturbation_coriolis.esm", "bindings": {"NLEV": "NLEV"},
   "expression_template_imports": [{"ref": "./tests/scmdyn_step900_state_inputs.esm"}, {"ref": "./tests/scmdyn_couple_cor_inputs.esm"}]},
  "Cur": {"ref": "../components/atmospheric_dynamics/wrf_arw/earth_curvature.esm", "bindings": {"NLEV": "NLEV"},
   "expression_template_imports": [{"ref": "./tests/scmdyn_step900_state_inputs.esm"}, {"ref": "./tests/scmdyn_couple_cur_inputs.esm"}]},
  "Ray": {"ref": "../components/atmospheric_dynamics/wrf_arw/rayleigh_damping.esm", "bindings": {"NLEV": "NLEV"},
   "expression_template_imports": [{"ref": "./tests/scmdyn_step900_state_inputs.esm"}, {"ref": "./tests/scmdyn_couple_ray_inputs.esm"}]},
  "ScmDynamicsColumn": {
   "variables": {
    "mu_p0": {"type": "parameter", "units": "Pa", "default": 0.0, "description": "Perturbation dry column mass mu' (WRF mu), prescribed."},
    "mu_b0": {"type": "parameter", "units": "Pa", "default": 79438.7, "description": "Base-state dry column mass (WRF mub), prescribed."},
    "p_top0": {"type": "parameter", "units": "Pa", "default": 17761.31, "description": "Lid pressure (WRF p_top), prescribed."},
    "f0": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1/s", "default": 8.899e-05, "description": "Coriolis parameter (WRF f), prescribed."},
    "e0": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1/s", "default": 0.00011554, "description": "Horizontal Coriolis parameter (WRF e), prescribed."},
    "sina0": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.0, "description": "Sine of the grid rotation, prescribed."},
    "cosa0": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 1.0, "description": "Cosine of the grid rotation, prescribed."},
    "dampcoef0": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1/s", "default": 0.003, "description": "Rayleigh damping coefficient, prescribed."},
    "zdamp0": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m", "default": 5000.0, "description": "Rayleigh damping depth, prescribed."},
    "mu_p": {"type": "unknown", "units": "Pa", "description": "mu' coupled into Geo and Vm."},
    "mu_b": {"type": "unknown", "units": "Pa", "description": "mu_b coupled into Geo and Vm."},
    "p_top": {"type": "unknown", "units": "Pa", "description": "p_top coupled into Geo."},
    "f": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1/s", "description": "f coupled into Cor."},
    "e": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1/s", "description": "e coupled into Cor."},
    "sina": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "description": "sina coupled into Cor."},
    "cosa": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "description": "cosa coupled into Cor."},
    "dampcoef": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1/s", "description": "dampcoef coupled into Ray."},
    "zdamp": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m", "description": "zdamp coupled into Ray."},
    "cor_du_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Cor.du_dt."},
    "cur_du_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Cur.du_dt."},
    "ray_du_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Ray.du_dt."},
    "cor_dv_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Cor.dv_dt."},
    "cur_dv_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Cur.dv_dt."},
    "ray_dv_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Ray.dv_dt."},
    "vm_dw_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Vm.dw_dt."},
    "cor_dw_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Cor.dw_dt."},
    "cur_dw_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Cur.dw_dt."},
    "ray_dw_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Ray.dw_dt."},
    "ray_dth_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "K/s", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Ray.dtheta_m_dt."},
    "vm_dphi_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m^2/s^3", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Vm.dphi_dt."},
    "geo_p_p_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "Pa", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Geo.p_p."},
    "du_dt": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Total non-physics tendency of u: Coriolis + curvature + Rayleigh damping."},
    "dv_dt": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Total non-physics tendency of v."},
    "dw_dt_nonpg": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Non-pressure part of the w tendency: Coriolis + curvature + Rayleigh damping."},
    "dw_dt": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Total w tendency: vertical pressure gradient and buoyancy + dw_dt_nonpg."},
    "dtheta_m_dt": {"type": "unknown", "units": "K/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Non-physics tendency of the moist potential temperature (the Rayleigh damper)."},
    "dphi_dt": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m^2/s^3", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Geopotential tendency g w."},
    "p_p": {"type": "unknown", "units": "Pa", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Perturbation pressure from the coupled equation of state."}
   },
   "equations": [
    {"lhs": "mu_p", "rhs": "mu_p0"}, {"lhs": "mu_b", "rhs": "mu_b0"}, {"lhs": "p_top", "rhs": "p_top0"},
    {"lhs": "f", "rhs": "f0"}, {"lhs": "e", "rhs": "e0"}, {"lhs": "sina", "rhs": "sina0"}, {"lhs": "cosa", "rhs": "cosa0"},
    {"lhs": "dampcoef", "rhs": "dampcoef0"}, {"lhs": "zdamp", "rhs": "zdamp0"},
    {"lhs": "du_dt", "rhs": {"op": "+", "args": ["cor_du_in", "cur_du_in", "ray_du_in"]}},
    {"lhs": "dv_dt", "rhs": {"op": "+", "args": ["cor_dv_in", "cur_dv_in", "ray_dv_in"]}},
    {"lhs": "dw_dt_nonpg", "rhs": {"op": "+", "args": ["cor_dw_in", "cur_dw_in", "ray_dw_in"]}},
    {"lhs": "dw_dt", "rhs": {"op": "+", "args": ["vm_dw_in", "dw_dt_nonpg"]}},
    {"lhs": "dtheta_m_dt", "rhs": "ray_dth_in"},
    {"lhs": "dphi_dt", "rhs": "vm_dphi_in"},
    {"lhs": "p_p", "rhs": "geo_p_p_in"}
   ],
   "tests": [
     {
       "id": "scm_dynamics_step900",
       "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU gfortran 13.3 REAL*4 build, dt = 60 s; data/eqwefic/scm_dyn) dumped by the ctessum-claude/WRF fork, branch earthsciml-instrumented, commit 83347b2 (rk_tendency, rk_step 1), merged with the same step's radiation subassembly dump and the wrfout eta grid (tools/merge_dumps.py -> data/eqwefic/dumps/dyn_column/esm_dump_dyn_suite_<step>.json). Expected values are the sums of the dumped mass-coupled increments of perturbation_coriolis, curvature, rk_rayleigh_damp and pg_buoy_w divided by the coupling mass of their grid point. Every mounted component receives the SAME dumped state; the geometry-derived inputs of the other four (interface heights, eta interpolation weights, perturbation pressure) come from the coupled WRFColumnGeometry, not from the dump. Measured residual in the standalone components at this step: Linf 1.2e-10 m/s^2 in du_dt (values <= 4.9e-4), 2.5e-11 in dv_dt, 2.2e-11 in the Coriolis w term, 4.9e-11 K/s in dtheta_m_dt, 0.012 Pa in p_p, rel 2.7e-8 in du_dt[1] and 1.5e-7 in dtheta_m_dt[59] -- identical to the standalone component tests, so the coupled geometry path adds nothing (its z_w agrees with WRF's z_at_w to 1.3e-7, its weights with fnm/fnp to 1.5e-8). Tolerances 5-10x above. The TOTAL w tendency is the exception: Linf 2.0e-4 m/s^2 against a profile maximum of 5.9e-4 (RMS 1.6e-4). That residual is the reference's, not the model's: WRF evaluates the equation of state in single precision, so its perturbation pressure p' carries 1.2-1.6e-2 Pa of rounding (the p_p assertion), and the vertical pressure-gradient term differentiates p' over a layer-centre spacing of ~0.0076 in eta, amplifying that rounding by g/(mu_d deta) ~ 0.016 m/s^2/Pa into a spurious w tendency of the same size as the physical one. Fed WRF's own dumped p', the same vertical-momentum component reproduces pg_buoy_w to 4.6e-9 m/s^2 (couplings-free test in components/atmospheric_dynamics/wrf_arw/vertical_momentum.esm). The total is therefore bounded only at abs 1e-3 m/s^2, which still fails any structural error (dropping mu' moves it by 1.2e-2, the moisture loading by 2.5e-2). Regime: step 900 (t = 15 h after 1999-10-22 19:00 UTC, pre-dawn deep stable night).",
       "parameter_overrides": {
         "mu_p0": -97.75,
         "mu_b0": 79363.078125,
         "p_top0": 17761.310546875,
         "f0": 8.898477972252294e-05,
         "e0": 0.00011554911179700866,
         "sina0": 0.0,
         "cosa0": 1.0,
         "dampcoef0": 0.003000000026077032,
         "zdamp0": 5000.0
       },
       "time_span": {
         "start": 0,
         "end": 1
       },
       "assertions": [
         {
